Once Shelene provides the URL and token, I can securely connect the RSVP form and submit a real end-to-end test entry into her sheet.

To configure it manually, open Shelene’s RSVP sheet and choose **Extensions → Apps Script**. Replace the starter code with the script below, set a private token, and deploy it as a web app. Then send me the resulting Web App URL and token so I can connect the RSVP form.

```javascript
const WEBHOOK_TOKEN = 'PASTE_A_LONG_PRIVATE_RANDOM_TOKEN_HERE';

function doPost(e) {
  const data = JSON.parse(e.postData.contents || '{}');
  if (data.token !== WEBHOOK_TOKEN) {
    return ContentService.createTextOutput('Unauthorized');
  }

  const spreadsheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const sheet = spreadsheet.getSheetByName('RSVPs') || spreadsheet.insertSheet('RSVPs');

  if (sheet.getLastRow() === 0) {
    sheet.appendRow(['Name', 'Phone Number', 'Guests', 'Submitted At']);
  }

  sheet.appendRow([
    data.name || '',
    data.phone || '',
    data.guestCount || '',
    data.submittedAt || new Date().toISOString()
  ]);

  return ContentService
    .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }))
    .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
}
```

In Apps Script, select **Deploy → New deployment → Web app**. Set **Execute as: Me** and **Who has access: Anyone**, then authorize and deploy. Copy the URL that ends in `/exec`. Keep both that URL and the token private; do not place them in Partiful or public invitations.

Here is the exact setup in **your** spreadsheet.

1. Open the Google Sheet where you want RSVP responses to appear.

2. In the menu, click **Extensions → Apps Script**. A new Apps Script tab opens.

3. Delete all starter code in the editor.

4. Paste this code:

```javascript
const WEBHOOK_TOKEN = 'REPLACE_THIS_WITH_A_LONG_PRIVATE_RANDOM_TOKEN';

function doPost(e) {
  try {
    const data = JSON.parse(e.postData.contents || '{}');

    if (data.token !== WEBHOOK_TOKEN) {
      return ContentService
        .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: 'Unauthorized' }))
        .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
    }

    const spreadsheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
    const sheet = spreadsheet.getSheetByName('RSVPs') || spreadsheet.insertSheet('RSVPs');

    if (sheet.getLastRow() === 0) {
      sheet.appendRow(['Name', 'Phone Number', 'Guests', 'Submitted At']);
      sheet.getRange('A1:D1').setFontWeight('bold');
      sheet.setFrozenRows(1);
    }

    sheet.appendRow([
      data.name || '',
      data.phone || '',
      data.guestCount || '',
      data.submittedAt || new Date().toISOString()
    ]);

    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  } catch (error) {
    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: String(error) }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  }
}
```

5. Replace `REPLACE_THIS_WITH_A_LONG_PRIVATE_RANDOM_TOKEN` with a long secret of your choice, such as a password-manager-generated token. Keep it private.

6. Click the **Save** icon. Give the project a clear name, such as `Sunset Open House RSVP Webhook`.

7. Click **Deploy → New deployment**.

8. In the deployment dialog, click the gear icon next to **Select type**, then choose **Web app**.

9. Set these exact options:

| Setting | Choose |
|---|---|
| Description | `Sunset RSVP webhook` |
| Execute as | **Me** |
| Who has access | **Anyone** |

10. Click **Deploy**. Google will ask you to authorize the script. Review the permissions and complete the authorization.

11. Copy the **Web app URL**. It should end with `/exec`.

12. Send me both of these privately in this chat:

| Send | Example |
|---|---|
| Web app URL | `https://script.google.com/macros/s/.../exec` |
| Private token | The secret you entered in Step 5 |

13. Finally, share the Google Sheet with Shelene: click **Share**, enter her email address, and choose **Viewer** or **Editor**. She will then see each RSVP that the website sends into the sheet.

Do **not** put the webhook URL or token into Partiful, the RSVP page, or a public message. Once you send them here, I can connect the RSVP form and submit a clearly labeled test entry to confirm it reaches the sheet.

Yes. This terminal-first workflow creates a **Google Sheets-bound Apps Script project**, generates a private token, uploads the webhook code, and opens the deployment screen. You only need to finish the Google authorization and choose the web-app access setting in the browser.

First, copy the **Sheet ID** from your new sheet’s URL. It is the text between `/d/` and `/edit`:

```text
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/SHEET_ID/edit
```

Then run these commands in your own Mac or PC terminal. Replace `PASTE_YOUR_NEW_SHEET_ID_HERE` only.

```bash
mkdir -p ~/sunset-rsvp-webhook
cd ~/sunset-rsvp-webhook

npm install --global @google/clasp
clasp login

clasp create "Sunset Open House RSVP Webhook" \
  --type sheets \
  --parentId "PASTE_YOUR_NEW_SHEET_ID_HERE"

TOKEN="$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
printf '%s\n' "$TOKEN" > webhook-token.txt
chmod 600 webhook-token.txt

cat > Code.gs <<EOF
const WEBHOOK_TOKEN = '$TOKEN';

function doPost(e) {
  try {
    const data = JSON.parse(e.postData.contents || '{}');

    if (data.token !== WEBHOOK_TOKEN) {
      return ContentService
        .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: 'Unauthorized' }))
        .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
    }

    const spreadsheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
    const sheet = spreadsheet.getSheetByName('RSVPs') || spreadsheet.insertSheet('RSVPs');

    if (sheet.getLastRow() === 0) {
      sheet.appendRow(['Name', 'Phone Number', 'Guests', 'Submitted At']);
      sheet.getRange('A1:D1').setFontWeight('bold');
      sheet.setFrozenRows(1);
    }

    sheet.appendRow([
      data.name || '',
      data.phone || '',
      data.guestCount || '',
      data.submittedAt || new Date().toISOString()
    ]);

    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  } catch (error) {
    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: String(error) }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  }
}
EOF

clasp push
clasp open-script
```

`clasp login` opens Google sign-in in your browser. The final command opens the new Apps Script project. In that browser tab, complete the last deployment step:

1. Click **Deploy → New deployment**.
2. Select **Web app**.
3. Set **Execute as: Me**.
4. Set **Who has access: Anyone**.
5. Click **Deploy** and complete Google authorization.
6. Copy the URL ending in `/exec`.

Then run this to show the private token you generated:

```bash
cat ~/sunset-rsvp-webhook/webhook-token.txt
```

Send me the `/exec` URL and that token privately. I will connect the RSVP form and submit one clearly labeled test RSVP.

> Keep `webhook-token.txt`, the token, and the `/exec` URL out of Partiful and any public post. The terminal flow uses the official `clasp create --type sheets --parentId ...`, `push`, and `open-script` commands for a spreadsheet-bound Apps Script project.[1]

### References

[1]: https://developers.google.com/apps-script/guides/clasp "Use the command-line interface with clasp"
[2]: https://developers.google.com/apps-script/guides/web "Deploy a script as a web app"

I need a brief manual step in the already-open Apps Script editor: the automation can open and deploy the project, but the code editor is not committing its source. Please take over the browser, click inside **Code.gs**, press **⌘A**, paste the code below, then press **⌘S**. Tell me when it shows **Saved to Drive**; I will immediately redeploy, test the RSVP log, and connect the website.

```javascript
function doPost(e) {
  const lock = LockService.getScriptLock();
  lock.waitLock(30000);
  try {
    const data = JSON.parse((e && e.postData && e.postData.contents) || '{}');
    const spreadsheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
    const sheet = spreadsheet.getSheetByName('RSVPs') || spreadsheet.insertSheet('RSVPs');

    if (sheet.getLastRow() === 0) {
      sheet.appendRow(['Name', 'Phone Number', 'Guests', 'Submitted At']);
      sheet.getRange('A1:D1').setFontWeight('bold');
      sheet.setFrozenRows(1);
    }

    sheet.appendRow([
      String(data.name || ''),
      String(data.phone || ''),
      Number(data.guestCount || 0),
      String(data.submittedAt || new Date().toISOString())
    ]);

    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  } catch (error) {
    return ContentService
      .createTextOutput(JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: String(error) }))
      .setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.JSON);
  } finally {
    lock.releaseLock();
  }
}
```

